# Redirect the bare root to the default language at the edge — instant
# HTTP redirect, before any JS downloads or runs. Previously this was a
# client-side redirect (React Router), which meant the browser had to
# download the full JS bundle, hydrate, and THEN navigate before any
# content painted — a major hit to LCP/FCP for anyone hitting the bare
# domain (which is the most common URL for people/tools to test).
# Matches the "x-default" hreflang, which already points to /en.
/  /en  302

/*  /index.html  200
